Spectroscopy is only useful if it changes what we build. We take the design rules
that come out of our materials work and apply them to devices: indoor photovoltaics that exceed
17% efficiency, fast near-infrared photodetectors from solution-processed AgBiS2, and scalable
direct X-ray detectors.

Indoor and low-light photovoltaics are a particular interest — the spectrum indoors is very
different from sunlight, and it rewards exactly the wide-bandgap, defect-tolerant absorbers we
study.
